<title>USA: Some investors may not grasp market risk-SEC chief.</title>
<headline>Some investors may not grasp market risk-SEC chief.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The top U.S. securities regulator voiced concern Wednesday about new investors who have only experienced a bull market and may react &quot;precipitously and carelessly&quot; in the face of a downturn in stock prices.</p>
<p>In the prepard text of a speech delivered in New York, Securities and Exchange Commission Chairman Arthur Levitt said many new investors were &quot;not as informed as they should be,&quot; a factor behind an agency push for better disclosure of potential risks of investing in mutual funds and other securities.</p>
</text>
